    "rich_text_7wRAHj": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_kKNUAG": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Do You Need a DTF Printer?",
            "heading_size": "h1"
          }
        },
        "text_R7gM8m": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Not necessarily.</p><p>There are two ways to work with DTF.</p><p>You can build your own production setup using a DTF printer, ink, film, powder, curing equipment, and a heat press.</p><p>Or you can simply order <strong>ready-to-press custom DTF transfers</strong>.</p><p>For creators and small businesses that don't want to maintain printing equipment, ordering transfers allows you to focus on designing, pressing, selling, and fulfilling apparel.</p><h2>Custom DTF Transfers vs. Gang Sheets: Which Should You Choose?</h2><p>Choose <strong>DTF Transfers by Size</strong> when you already know the finished dimensions you need and want an easy way to order individual transfers.</p><p>Choose a <strong>DTF Gang Sheet</strong> when you want to fit multiple designs or multiple copies onto a larger sheet.</p><p>A simple way to think about it is:</p><p><strong>Individual sizes → convenience</strong></p><p><strong>Gang sheets → maximize your available sheet space</strong></p><p>Both options can work well—the right choice depends on how you produce your apparel.</p><h2>Getting Started With DTF Transfers</h2><p>If you're ready to try DTF, the process can be straightforward:</p><ol><li>Prepare your artwork.</li><li>Choose your transfer size or gang sheet.</li><li>Upload your design.</li><li>Select your quantity.</li><li>Receive your ready-to-press transfers.</li><li>Heat press them onto your garments according to the supplied application instructions.</li></ol><p>You don't need to master the entire DTF printing process to start creating professional custom apparel.</p>"
          }
        },
